    "instruction": "Write a small adaptive investigator. Use the functions, callers and downstream obligation to find what the parent overlooks. Consider a wrong readout of sufficient state, a wrong update, or genuinely missing information; do not assume any one diagnosis. Choose a legal native query that could reveal the issue. Return the normal query plus, when useful, a compact note stating the obligation, suspected boundary/assumption, evidence and proposed change. Your note is a hypothesis; measured results decide whether there is a defect. You may propose removing or bypassing a decomposition. Avoid duplicate queries; null stops. Up to eight native query slots are available.",
